",\"A\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"C\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"B\",\"A\",\"A\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"A\",\"B\",\"B\",\"B\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"A\",\"A\",\"B\",\"B\",\"B\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"A\",\"B\",\"B\",\"B\",\"B\",\"C\",\"C\",\"C\",\"B\",\"B\",\"B\",\"B\"],\"pairs\":[[0,1],[0,5],[0,6],[1,2],[1,6],[1,7],[2,3],[2,7],[2,8],[3,4],[3,8],[3,9],[4,9],[4,10],[5,6],[5,12],[5,13],[6,7],[6,13],[6,14],[7,8],[7,14],[7,15],[8,9],[8,15],[8,16],[9,10],[9,16],[9,17],[10,11],[10,17],[10,18],[11,18],[11,19],[12,13],[12,22],[12,23],[13,14],[13,23],[13,24],[14,15],[14,24],[14,25],[15,16],[15,25],[16,17],[17,18],[17,26],[18,19],[18,26],[18,27],[19,20],[19,27],[19,28],[20,21],[20,28],[20,29],[21,29],[21,30],[22,23],[22,32],[22,33],[23,24],[23,33],[23,34],[24,25],[24,34],[24,35],[25,35],[25,36],[26,27],[26,37],[26,38],[27,28],[27,38],[27,39],[28,29],[28,39],[28,40],[29,30],[29,40],[29,41],[30,31],[30,41],[30,42],[31,42],[31,43],[32,33],[32,44],[33,34],[33,44],[33,45],[34,35],[34,45],[34,46],[35,36],[35,46],[35,47],[36,47],[36,48],[37,38],[37,49],[37,50],[38,39],[38,50],[38,51],[39,40],[39,51],[39,52],[40,41],[40,52],[40,53],[41,42],[41,53],[41,54],[42,43],[42,54],[42,55],[43,55],[43,56],[44,45],[44,57],[44,58],[45,46],[45,58],[45,59],[46,47],[46,59],[46,60],[47,48],[47,60],[47,61],[48,49],[48,61],[48,62],[49,50],[49,62],[49,63],[50,51],[50,63],[50,64],[51,52],[51,64],[51,65],[52,53],[52,65],[52,66],[53,54],[53,66],[53,67],[54,55],[54,67],[54,68],[55,56],[55,68],[55,69],[56,69],[56,70],[57,58],[57,71],[58,59],[58,71],[58,72],[59,60],[59,72],[59,73],[60,61],[60,73],[60,74],[61,62],[61,74],[61,75],[62,63],[62,75],[62,76],[63,64],[63,76],[63,77],[64,65],[64,77],[64,78],[65,66],[65,78],[65,79],[66,67],[66,79],[66,80],[67,68],[67,80],[67,81],[68,69],[68,81],[68,82],[69,70],[69,82],[69,83],[70,83],[71,72],[71,84],[72,73],[72,84],[72,85],[73,74],[73,85],[73,86],[74,75],[74,86],[74,87],[75,76],[75,87],[75,88],[76,77],[76,88],[76,89],[77,78],[77,89],[77,90],[78,79],[78,90],[78,91],[79,80],[79,91],[79,92],[80,81],[80,92],[80,93],[81,82],[81,93],[81,94],[82,83],[82,94],[82,95],[83,95],[84,85],[84,96],[85,86],[85,96],[85,97],[86,87],[86,97],[86,98],[87,88],[87,98],[87,99],[88,89],[88,99],[88,100],[89,90],[89,100],[89,101],[90,91],[90,101],[90,102],[91,92],[91,102],[91,103],[92,93],[92,103],[92,104],[93,94],[93,104],[93,105],[94,95],[94,105],[94,106],[95,106],[96,97],[96,107],[97,98],[97,107],[97,108],[98,99],[98,108],[98,109],[99,100],[99,109],[99,110],[100,101],[100,110],[100,111],[101,102],[101,111],[101,112],[102,103],[102,112],[102,113],[103,104],[103,113],[103,114],[104,105],[104,114],[104,115],[105,106],[105,115],[105,116],[106,116],[107,108],[107,117],[108,109],[108,117],[108,118],[109,110],[109,118],[109,119],[110,111],[110,119],[110,120],[111,112],[111,120],[111,121],[112,113],[112,121],[112,122],[113,114],[113,122],[113,123],[114,115],[114,123],[114,124],[115,116],[115,124],[117,118],[118,119],[118,125],[119,120],[119,125],[119,126],[120,121],[120,126],[120,127],[121,122],[121,127],[121,128],[122,123],[122,128],[123,124],[125,126],[126,127],[127,128]],\"counts\":[[174,26,30],[26,138,26],[30,26,202]]}],\"profiles\":[[0.376119402985075,0.0895522388059701,0,0.0895522388059701,0.262686567164179,0.0388059701492537,0,0.0388059701492537,0.104477611940299],[0.338709677419355,0.104838709677419,0,0.104838709677419,0.213709677419355,0.0524193548387097,0,0.0524193548387097,0.133064516129032],[0.256637168141593,0.0383480825958702,0.0442477876106195,0.0383480825958702,0.20353982300885,0.0383480825958702,0.0442477876106195,0.0383480825958702,0.297935103244838]],\"distance\":[[0,0.0738473781246737,0.253692780138662],[0.0738473781246737,0,0.217198929590176],[0.253692780138662,0.217198929590176,0]],\"similarity\":[[1,0.708910209883345,0],[0.708910209883345,1,0.143850568110531],[0,0.143850568110531,1]]}\n</script>\n\n## Example data\n\nOur walkthrough uses simulated tissue on a hexagonal grid with spots colored\naccording to their label (\"A\", \"B\", or \"C\"), which we can pretend represents\ncell type. Whilst this setting most closely resembles standard-definition\nVisium, the explanations also apply to the other technologies.\n\n::: {.algorithm-figure data-figure=\"spots\"}\n:::\n\n## 1. Finding neighbors\n\nFirst, neighborhood relationships between cells are computed. This process is\ncovered in more detail in [Neighborhoods](neighborhoods.qmd). For our purposes\nin this example, we form a _connection_ between a spot and the six spots that\nsurround it.\n\n::: {.algorithm-figure data-figure=\"links\"}\n:::\n\n## 2. Count connections\n\nNext, we count the number of connections that link each pair of labels,\nproducing a label × label table for each sample. Each connection is counted in\nboth directions: an `A`–`B` connection adds one to both the `A`–`B` and `B`–`A`\ncounts, and an `A`–`A` connection increments the `A`–`A` count by two.\n\n::: {.algorithm-figure data-figure=\"counts\"}\n:::\n\n## 3. Normalization (optional)\n\nBy default, `normalize` is true, which means that each sample's connection\ncounts are divided by their total (i.e. they are converted to proportions\ninstead of raw counts). This allows sample size (i.e. number of occupied spots\n/ cells) to be controlled: two samples with similar spatial characteristics but\nof different sizes will still have a high similarity score.\n\n::: {.algorithm-figure data-figure=\"profile\"}\n:::\n\n## 4. Calculate similarities\n\nThe dissimilarity between two samples is calculated as the Euclidean distance\nbetween their connection counts/proportions. We normalize distances by dividing\neach by the largest.\n\n::: {.algorithm-figure data-figure=\"compare\"}\n:::\n\nFinally, we convert distances to similarity scores by subtracting each from 1:\n\n$$s_{ij} = 1 - \\frac{d_{ij}}{\\max d}$$\n\n\nA similarity of 1 means that two samples have identical profiles, whilst 0\ncorresponds to the least similar pair.\n\n::: {.algorithm-figure data-figure=\"similarity\"}\n:::\n\n## Options\n\n### Only transitions\n\nSetting `only_transitions` to true drops connections between spots/cells with\nthe same label. This means that similarity scores only represent\ncharacteristics of borders between labels.\n\n::: {.algorithm-figure data-figure=\"transitions\"}\n:::\n\n### Pools\n\n`pools` groups samples, for example replicates, and sums their connection\ncounts before distances are calculated, effectively treating each pool as a\nsingle sample.\n\n::: {.algorithm-figure data-figure=\"pools\"}\n:::\n",
